    "amount": "900",
    "amountNumeric": 900,
    "description": "Permatours chose to support Brooks because their work exemplifies the spirit of mutual aid, bioregional resilience, and community-rooted transformation that aligns with our mission. As a trusted facilitator and organizer, Brooks has consistently shown up for communities across the East Coast—from New Orleans to Atlanta, from Rochester to Midcoast Maine—co-creating mutual aid infrastructure, supporting jailhouse lawyers, increasing access to clean water, and holding space for transformative justice.\n\nBrooks’ contributions are often behind the scenes and unpaid, yet deeply impactful. They work tirelessly to weave connections, hold healing and organizing spaces, and meet people where they are. Their presence strengthens the social fabric in places often overlooked or underserved.\n\nWe are supporting Brooks in this moment to help them regain reliable transportation—a vital tool for continuing their grassroots work. After their vehicle broke down while volunteering with Cooperate WNC to strengthen post-disaster mutual aid networks, they became stranded without the resources to recover on their own. With this support, Brooks will be able to repair their vehicle, return to Midcoast Maine to recover their camper-home, and resume their commitments in Western North Carolina, where they are co-facilitating community-building circles.\n\nPermatours believes that investing in individuals like Brooks is a direct investment in regenerative systems, mutual aid networks, and the decentralized leadership we need for a just and abundant future. This contribution is a small way to return the care that Brooks has extended so generously across communities. We hope it enables them to continue seeding resilience, solidarity, and healing wherever they go.",
    "recipientNotified": "Yes",
    "learnings": "",
    "coordinates": {
      "lat": 34.2189515,
      "lng": -80.2599081
    }
