    "description": "We gave funds to Permatours because they organize work parties that build infrastructure on permaculture projects across the Northeast US, such as building a cobb oven, hempcrete tiny homes, garden beds, and much more. These events educate regional community members on building techniques and permaculture methods, while meeting needs of local community centers and businesses, while building relationships across people, projects, and techniques for community inter-reliance. Their impacts are described in full in their impact report stories which can be read at https://bloomnetwork.earth/permatours . \n\nYou can also scroll just the impacts reported, in list form, at https://bloomnetwork.earth/impacts\n\nHere are a few highlights: \"Empowered a local mutual aid food network to expand their offerings through community meals.\"\n\nStrengthened food sovereignty efforts by connecting growing, foraging, and cooking.\n\nSupported the launch of a tree nursery that will provide long-term food security infrastructure.\n\nEmpowered youth through hands-on participation in regenerative practices.\n\nConstructed a wildlife pond & tree guilds to enhance local biodiversity. Extended walking paths to integrate with the Traditional Plants\n\nAnd so much more!!!",
